{"title":"Miquel's point","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Miquel_and_Steiner&#39;s_quadrilateral_theorem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Miquel and Steiner's quadrilateral theorem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Circle_of_circumcenters\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Circle of circumcenters</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Triangle_of_circumcenters\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Triangle of circumcenters</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Analogue_of_Miquel&#39;s_point\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Analogue of Miquel's point</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Six_circles_crossing_point\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Six circles crossing point</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Triple_of_the_circumcenters_and_symmetry\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Triple of the circumcenters and symmetry</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span id=\"Miquel_and_Steiner.27s_quadrilateral_theorem\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Miquel_and_Steiner's_quadrilateral_theorem\">Miquel and Steiner's quadrilateral theorem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Miquel%27s_point&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Miquel and Steiner&#39;s quadrilateral theorem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:4_Miquel_circles.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/2b/4_Miquel_circles.png/500px-4_Miquel_circles.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"500\" height=\"328\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/2b/4_Miquel_circles.png/750px-4_Miquel_circles.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/2b/4_Miquel_circles.png/1000px-4_Miquel_circles.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let four lines made four triangles of a complete quadrilateral. In the diagram these are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/5/d15ba44fecfa3229692453358049c41718818e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC, \\triangle ADE, \\triangle CEF, \\triangle BDF.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"264\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Prove that the circumcircles of all four triangles meet at a single point.\n</p><p><i><b>Proof</b></i>\n</p><p>Let circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> cross the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/9/979c6deb11752ef4146e52440d2955ee0beead13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CEF$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/8/3a8a14533852c3d530dbfa98fa32b2a7a6f0e9b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M.$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> cross <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> second time in the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/0/4e037912024535666d4f5194dcf67a6231061c8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G.$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/b/bebdb0068b0094b62333c9d53df21fcdde13ca4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CMGF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/7/2e7c4f1a832f6534c8d24962e31f16c3f8a847af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies \\angle BCM = \\angle MGF.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"196\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/c/89c701f39bc54e432a19b52e651530a0425a755b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AMCB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/0/4f096f2ae800c80e6f766641e4f97ca1f199f7b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies \\angle BCM + \\angle BAM = 180^\\circ \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"294\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/e/afeda894f598a40a3909e88c7ab2f005f71e8338.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAG + \\angle AGF = 180^\\circ \\implies AB||GF.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"313\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/9/fd964461bb91fd13c92ff47598543729fe27f808.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EMGF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/a/f2a6362e04a12f14f783c1c310159711103a0e4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies \\angle AME = \\angle EFG.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"192\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/1/4f1f25cbad7efd7a4d7cf6b8f0061761b748eb45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD||GF \\implies \\angle ADE + \\angle DFG = 180^\\circ \\implies \\angle ADE + \\angle AME = 180^\\circ \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"606\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/8/bd812e8333ae3a6987b98d337c0a784f95890fbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADEM$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" /> is cyclic and circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/0/db041d9c0fda44cf24b4f4ae7f02243ef2ea7f92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADE$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> contain the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/8/3a8a14533852c3d530dbfa98fa32b2a7a6f0e9b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M.$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Similarly circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/c/4bc4a1ecf2193896680e5e73b698d50e779548b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BDF$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> contain the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> as desired.\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Circle_of_circumcenters\">Circle of circumcenters</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Miquel%27s_point&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Circle of circumcenters\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Miquel_point.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/8e/Miquel_point.png/450px-Miquel_point.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"450\" height=\"265\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/8e/Miquel_point.png/675px-Miquel_point.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/8e/Miquel_point.png/900px-Miquel_point.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let four lines made four triangles of a complete quadrilateral. In the diagram these are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/5/d15ba44fecfa3229692453358049c41718818e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC, \\triangle ADE, \\triangle CEF, \\triangle BDF.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"264\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Prove that the circumcenters of all four triangles and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> are concyclic.\n</p><p><i><b>Proof</b></i>\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/e/1ee865c65e5a2047acc487fcbfb6f74c6f26cab9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega, \\omega, \\Omega&#39;,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/0/0f0b5243f7e525a53836ea34c8a49486dace660f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega&#39;$\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the circumcircles of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/2/d32f852760a1c0a3f5bc89a4fc660b3f29bd5a47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC, \\triangle CEF, \\triangle BDF,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"197\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/0/1a070d4bf8bcf8e36ef3f368ab964c052a1c2eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADE,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"17\" /> respectively.\n</p><p>In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/b/feb9a8bb8986d22f99f162f3e2112440738e5395.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega&#39; \\angle MDF = \\angle MBF.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"170\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/4/0f47b3d8ebf8b5008b1556c19cd8ae111bc5344b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega&#39; \\angle MDE = \\frac {\\overset{\\Large\\frown} {ME}} {2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"148\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/a/d1a30c9c946a561bfb130894432aa55948d58b0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ME$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> is the common chord of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/8/488bd752ce720e866d8f1808d33003fb646f3de1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega&#39; \\implies \\angle MOE = \\overset{\\Large\\frown} {ME} \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"232\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/0/7600e979ad700ba71e634ce843ba155ec6a53bb4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle MO&#39;o&#39; = \\frac {\\overset{\\Large\\frown} {ME}} {2} =  \\angle MDE.\\]\" width=\"217\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/1/551fab3023436463570c8159f37571740d523aa7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MF$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> is the common chord of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/a/b8af9fb99901a02dc099b87bc0d8063682561ddc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega&#39; \\implies  \\angle MDF = \\angle Moo&#39; = \\angle MO&#39;o&#39;.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"305\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/5/4d5ee546f7ea84755eae7a58fbf1d892bd258118.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MC$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> is the common chord of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bac68e47885d50a1caea609d1636e2b9a85bd7a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega&#39; \\implies  \\angle MBC = \\angle MOo&#39; \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"258\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/9/c4940766e30de1f476a0e5f923dce15c1cb13892.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle MOo&#39; = \\angle MO&#39;o&#39; \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"196\" height=\"16\" /> points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/d/57d88c7790bc6ee110ad9f9fea5b4cd10ddbacc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M, O, O&#39;, o,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/3/423715bd1b51cd6fff3d03f9ba98e10395a6c2d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$o&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"16\" /> are concyclic as desired.\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Triangle_of_circumcenters\">Triangle of circumcenters</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Miquel%27s_point&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Triangle of circumcenters\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Miquel_perspector.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/c/c6/Miquel_perspector.png/500px-Miquel_perspector.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"500\" height=\"322\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/c/c6/Miquel_perspector.png/750px-Miquel_perspector.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/c/c6/Miquel_perspector.png/1000px-Miquel_perspector.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let four lines made four triangles of a complete quadrilateral.\n</p><p>In the diagram these are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/5/d15ba44fecfa3229692453358049c41718818e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC, \\triangle ADE, \\triangle CEF, \\triangle BDF.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"264\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Let points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/2/3227e5c10b934ca807ad964b350af2e6aa83327f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O,O_A, O_B,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/2/be2b7d9af12c551508264ff8ed054503c4e1b890.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> be the circumcenters of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/d/65d67d7b126e182494956777e6f3bf208983f713.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC, \\triangle ADE, \\triangle BDF,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"199\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/1/661a39ce1626acc26216acc56960bf2038e285f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CEF,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" /> respectively.\n</p><p>Prove that  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/e/a7eda82065a8621a27b8fa992c69b99b50d8415c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle O_AO_BO_C \\sim \\triangle ABC,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" /> and perspector of these triangles point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is the second (different from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />) point of intersection <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/3/ce37053e41c099a6a717782782815c04748ac7db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega \\cap \\Theta,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> is circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/2/a321d1b883ba985b1f59ca076beaaf17aa8ab06c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f07921ebf307f8caa624efa73017475baf34d7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle O_AO_BO_C.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><i><b>Proof</b></i>\n</p><p>Quadrungle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/6/706c615278b78bbee8c176bf6d9a0f9b45f11ed2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MECF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/1/cb18f2d5d57313a66c31a512fead5d75e7404fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies \\angle AEM = \\angle BFM \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"237\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/8/128b242a6fd4145b73db3298a9f949112a2f530e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle AO_AM = 2\\angle AEM = 2 \\angle BFM = \\angle BO_BM.\\]\" width=\"358\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/b/96be27dd53e4d918b1439a72697819b85ed8b474.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle CO_CM = 2\\angle CFM = 2 \\angle BFM = \\angle BO_BM.\\]\" width=\"359\" height=\"15\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/c/afc4cbc98a40d847f7d7d8d8aca49331eb0bac9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO_A = MO_A, BO_B = MO_B, CO_C = MO_C \\implies \\triangle AO_AM \\sim \\triangle BO_BM \\sim \\triangle CO_CM.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"669\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Spiral similarity centered at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> with rotation angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/0/e30ffc82db304137d0883381954f3b8ea5367b7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AMO_A = \\angle BMO_B = CMO_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"252\" height=\"17\" /> and the coefficient of homothety <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/2/0629292b08ef7f924d3a74a031e269d583f19ebf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {AM}{MO_A} = \\frac {BM}{MO_B} =\\frac {CM}{MO_C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"196\" height=\"42\" /> mapping <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/8/4d8aa423de2031c09aa06a1687767414dbb8120d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/0/0e0af44578003bbd64382d00ed07ed2e33099284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/4/914e5487e2047aeb69098ae3955471d44bc821bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_C \\implies \\triangle O_AO_BO_C \\sim \\triangle ABC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"255\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/c/fcc45157aa740e17d88eb1b86e7f202fba4331c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AO_AM, \\triangle BO_BM, \\triangle CO_CM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"241\" height=\"18\" /> are triangles in double perspective at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/e/7be18121befa1996a376fd26285b0a92321dd98d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>These triangles are in triple perspective <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/f/09f96bbd8d54591dc7d76e4f2613cc8b679fc230.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies AO_A, BO_B, CO_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" /> are concurrent at the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/f/87fa832bf21ebc48a46289cd7aea73ffcc84c111.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X.$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>The rotation angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/d/10dbf7eb06add38f18240a2205f295184875ce81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AO_AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/c/14cf75978166234b5d073b429c0e746bf99c7092.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BO_BM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/b/62b2c1a03d069023544c75e03bfa4a3a975908ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle O_AMO_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"17\" /> for sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/6/1e6b59da68d6612e13f0bc44d5816b0625168d60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/e/3cec35d174d6f591219b7a0d3ae04d148604688b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_BM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"17\" /> or angle between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/7/057717d6cb8791c6523112ec90347a6b730802d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/d/79d49c28e37ce4aa15cb48aaf882ceedbc004aac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BO_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"38\" height=\"15\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/0/690e9e7f09867510674d129a76af8e15895e5707.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AXB \\implies M O_AO_BX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"195\" height=\"17\" /> is cyclic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/563742840fd26b5545275e5fb04911909e0d924a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies M O_AO_BXO_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"17\" /> is cyclic.\n</p><p>Therefore  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/6/4b64c1838c9aa3763e0993ff9a17d07af8af95da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle O_AXO_B = \\angle  O_AO_CO_B = \\angle ACB \\implies ABCX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"382\" height=\"17\" /> is cyclic as desired.\n</p><p>Similarly, one can prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/7/da74d74d875a9a50323d42d4a01ef97944e639a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADE \\sim \\triangle OO_BO_C, \\triangle BDF \\sim \\triangle OO_AO_C, \\triangle CEF \\sim \\triangle OO_AO_B.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"517\" height=\"18\" /> \n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Double_perspective_triangles\" title=\"Double perspective triangles\">Double perspective triangles</a></li></ul>\n<p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Analogue_of_Miquel.27s_point\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Analogue_of_Miquel's_point\">Analogue of Miquel's point</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Miquel%27s_point&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Analogue of Miquel&#39;s point\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:5_circles.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/08/5_circles.png/400px-5_circles.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"371\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/08/5_circles.png/600px-5_circles.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/0/08/5_circles.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let inscribed quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/066c122a1654c7dbeb8526c1321ae9a8ad45163b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABB&#39;A&#39;$\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" /> and \n</p><p>points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/5/17590090920b227c64b59553cc9b9b0b8f79929d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C \\in AB&#39;, C&#39; \\in A&#39;B&#39;, D \\in A&#39;B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"237\" height=\"19\" /> be given.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/1/7e1b7d94789826169521b02b72984416dde7742c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\theta = \\odot CC&#39;B&#39;, \\Theta = \\odot BDD&#39;, M = \\theta \\cap \\Theta,\\]\" width=\"310\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/9/8f91df5fd6e4b20fe9df1da84d0d78fb228c9616.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[E = C&#39;D \\cap \\odot B&#39;CC&#39;, D&#39; = AB \\cap CE, F = CC&#39; \\cap DD&#39;.\\]\" width=\"429\" height=\"17\" />\nProve that points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/0/8108105f9527e2e56f49b390f7aa8fc8f47776cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B, B&#39;,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> are concyclic.\n</p><p><i><b>Proof</b></i>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/d/eed75f478fe690045b68f8fdc6b37eea3d9d80b9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle BMB&#39; =  \\angle EMB&#39; - \\angle EMB =  \\angle ECB&#39; - \\angle ED&#39;B  = \\angle BAB&#39; \\blacksquare\\]\" width=\"507\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><i><b>Corollary</b></i>\n</p><p>The points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/a/d7aa65689906234e3567cb8775e539b6fa9dd355.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F, C, D&#39;,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> are concyclic.\n</p><p>The points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/7/927a3ce05c0fc3469249259cf6a581241e848bb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F, C&#39;, D,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> are concyclic.\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Six_circles_crossing_point\">Six circles crossing point</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Miquel%27s_point&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Six circles crossing point\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Fixed_Miquel_point.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/7/7f/Fixed_Miquel_point.png/410px-Fixed_Miquel_point.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"410\" height=\"317\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/7/7f/Fixed_Miquel_point.png/615px-Fixed_Miquel_point.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/7/7f/Fixed_Miquel_point.png/820px-Fixed_Miquel_point.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/8/6f8dcf98ed1b21dbc446aa28d097d4281599c25e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" /> point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/8/ea89f646684e08d8d724a7c7f09ca49aeda2e9df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P \\in BC,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" /> point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/5/055d2262c50545ec89aa9cfe3348587b28b26423.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X \\in \\Omega = \\odot ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"135\" height=\"16\" /> be given.\n</p><p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/d/32de2919513564ab4ac3003b5b00fe3cd64c434a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y = PX \\cap \\Omega, D = AX \\cap BC, E = AY \\cap BC,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"359\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/9/40939f118a4cefae96ea73c601da810903697fe1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\omega = \\odot ADE, \\theta = \\odot PEY, \\Theta = \\odot PDX,\\]\" width=\"299\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/f/cef1035739eda1d37fd50c34f758a1d839b37cc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sigma = \\odot BP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" /> tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/1/6118415c7ec651766445020ddba8f7937ffb4e9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB, \\Sigma = \\odot CP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"18\" /> tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/0/3a0b75202202b36c2a62a22bba07fc06501bea7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Prove that the circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/a/bfa25c95b2d2a3cf5594fe9134b70bb23bbcefa6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega, \\Omega, \\theta, \\Theta, \\sigma,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/f/c8f77e3035db5fe9a4975967750ac1a6454bda8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Sigma$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> have the common point.\n</p><p><i><b>Proof</b></i> \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659f280679c16d19e35f74eba9923b09cd3b58be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M = \\omega \\cap \\Omega \\ne A.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"18\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/4/714b4ead3739dfe49d61101876038f113c4900bc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle YCM = \\angle YXM = \\angle YAM = \\angle EAM = \\angle EDM \\implies\\]\" width=\"443\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/d/71dd13dd3a4d7a4e86f3d93c2d7ca2ef44040d46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PDM = \\angle PXM \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"196\" height=\"14\" /> points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/7/ba7d61f95e5f2c4f6af4f5db40473d6a058fee50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M,P,D,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> are concyclic, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/8/f58dc27eb4abfd1d18cf90a448dc56b0d4f40c10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M \\in \\Theta.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" /> Similarly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/f/43f0f1bb3b58ee2d1074487116b09eba8588bcb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M \\in \\theta, M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" /> is the Miquel point of quadrungle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/7/127313e21488cfbd1eeedbb4088aecefb64eaad6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EDXY.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/f/c4f8e8e9b84344deea705fd1e12ea0ca21d362cf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle CMY = 180^\\circ - \\angle CAB - \\angle BAY.\\]\" width=\"276\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/3/6d3ffa305ccf7ea13f5a3c7b1b2b748823011d11.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle PMY = \\angle PEY = \\angle ABC - \\angle BAY.\\]\" width=\"299\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/a/94af22a60c10695f6ca76b7c3f654faaebff04d0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle PMC = \\angle CMY - \\angle PMY = (180^\\circ - \\angle CAB - \\angle BAY) - (\\angle ABC - \\angle BAY) = \\angle ACB.\\]\" width=\"671\" height=\"18\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/b/06b4f14c0c09af1084b20a2b1abe32d547cf8e77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PMC = \\angle ACB \\implies AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"220\" height=\"14\" /> is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/2/222c3654ce639498f116004f5f24d95283a92752.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Sigma.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/7/9d7db0369f72d5b55dc846d18ea4371175e034a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sigma.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" />\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Triple_of_the_circumcenters_and_symmetry\">Triple of the circumcenters and symmetry</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Miquel%27s_point&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Triple of the circumcenters and symmetry\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> inside it be given. Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/c/69c458d59e6fd04565638e690bd3b7eeaae01da4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega = \\odot BCP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" /> centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/b/d4bd854b8682640212866fdbc453a4b45d3df912.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D, \\theta = \\odot ACP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" /> centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/a/adac2313a9adfc2cf184f4e7d21350e75e3a02c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E, \\varphi = \\odot ABP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" /> centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/9/f2920fa2bc40ed68149a854f8b32c09f619b0d70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F.$\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" />\nLet point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9d1d557cf040f68ba9a645530f0e4ad86df696d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X_a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> is symmetric <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> with respect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/1/8018e5e78e7b800ed9c1aea457e1f5f44927536b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC, X_b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> is symmetric <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with respect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/9/949e4389c8e325b4277ea4ddcd207d756ec1e88b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC, X_c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> is symmetric <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with respect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ecee609050b0744995a1b79ec0fcd162a97441b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB.$\" width=\"32\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Prove that \n</p><p>1) circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/b/d2ba0fea23adc53d3cdb6f1cc8c3a1072b3942bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega&#39;, \\theta&#39;,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/7/b97ebc89613561cf3ec26768b8f090c7d17cf3fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\varphi&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"19\" /> have the common point.\n</p><p>2) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/a/19ae7f42bbea2c035a7d8272f4d2e79faac04e25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEF \\sim \\triangle X_aX_bX_c.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"174\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2026_f_10_7b.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/8c/2026_f_10_7b.png/350px-2026_f_10_7b.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"350\" height=\"286\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/8c/2026_f_10_7b.png/525px-2026_f_10_7b.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/8c/2026_f_10_7b.png/700px-2026_f_10_7b.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p><i><b>Proof</b></i>\n</p><p>1) Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/2/bc218972074cbbd507423a84ed6732514682a80b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q = \\omega&#39; \\cap \\theta&#39;.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b3017575d1116ea559c198180821edcf0af1fa15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overset{\\Large\\frown} {BQC} &gt; \\overset{\\Large\\frown} {BC}, \\overset{\\Large\\frown} {AQC} &gt; \\overset{\\Large\\frown} {AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"201\" height=\"27\" /> as shown on diagram.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/3406a370b92014a5485f49ea333302910075bf16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overset{\\Large\\frown} {BPC} = \\overset{\\Large\\frown} {BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"98\" height=\"24\" /> where first arc of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and second arc of  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/a/34a7a1647a74f05a398f51f9f9855c0e70ba5f0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega&#39;,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"19\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/a/72ac36d80984c4976e82469118ae91786f9022b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BQC + \\angle BPC = 180^\\circ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"200\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Similarly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/4/314eaa47b4adc9035ee4aca22e751b6d563f2a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AQC + \\angle APC = 180^\\circ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"198\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/c/37c2257c8d44d8600be3fa07f7f0406833c7ae12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AQB = \\angle AQC + \\angle BQC = 360^\\circ - \\angle APC - \\angle BPC = \\angle APB \\implies Q \\in \\varphi&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"612\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>2) Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on bisector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/4/7d4657c543c802576669890d5d3e92a2d506f2ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PB,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on bisector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/0/6701facf8cc0f6b6310fcb025811f294a13fae94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PC,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/d/53d454afdb04730f5f5f99a4fa9ba21a61676883.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle EDF = 180^\\circ - \\angle BPC = \\angle BQC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"281\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9d1d557cf040f68ba9a645530f0e4ad86df696d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X_a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/f/aafdbfcdfa2b5de7686ecaf360a747ee5cdca584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X_c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" /> lies on bisector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/5/375c4850082f1ea5f746a376272b00cb7d761384.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QB,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" />  points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9d1d557cf040f68ba9a645530f0e4ad86df696d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X_a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/0/680da2cd6368d2917f9f5b0664aff76aa8d4c6f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X_b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" /> lies on bisector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/7/fc7b33bbcf754b0faa2b91e163a1af5ecc9af170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QC,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/9/4d93969159582150195ec855df11b1b99e0fba41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle X_bX_aX_c = \\angle BQC = \\angle EDF.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"246\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/5/285741fe9477e5a7d7b27f11099bf8293e0ae560.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle X_aX_bX_c = \\angle AQC = \\angle DEF. \\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"259\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018095700\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.069 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.089 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 745/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 30477/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:23470:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018095700 and revision id 291946. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}